you're the batman so you're fast  justice league snyder cut is eight years  in the making  and what in eight years it's been from  tragedy to fan campaigns and everything  in between  the production of this four-part movie  is basically a film itself  so what did the behind the scenes of  this hbo cut look like  and how close did snyder really come to  filming the batman and joker scene in  his own backyard  snyder cut isn't just an added bonus for  fans of the dc universe  there's a deeper meaning and reasoning  as to why the film was even made  but first let's dive into how they  actually brought the film to life  i mean we have to try don't we we have  to try  we could all agree that jason momoa has  been a truly epic  addition to dc hands down but when we  found out what it actually looks like  when he's filming his water scenes  we couldn't hold back our laughter take  a look  it's just such a drastic difference from  what we see in the final version that we  couldn't help but be taken aback  apparently jason had no control of his  body when he was filming these scenes  he was attached to a robotic arm and rig  so they could coordinate his movements  the way they wanted  the best part they had to tie his hair  back into a hair net so they could use  vfx to really control the way it moved  underneath the water  kudos to momoa on this one and then you  look back at him  if you think momoa had it bad while  filming those scenes he's also admitted  that going to the washroom wasn't the  easiest while wearing his costume  and his trident well that would leave  him sore for days after a shoot that  involved fighting with it  but that's just the tip of the iceberg  when it comes to how uncomfortable the  justice league's costumes can be  amber heard literally had to be vacuum  sealed into her mirror suit  and the first time ezra miller put on  the flash costume it was so constricting  he couldn't even lift his arm over his  head  yeah i  i need friends just by looking at wonder  woman's suit  you can tell it's not the most  comfortable thing to be in  but listen to gal gadot recount just how  excruciating it was to wear  it was so tight and i literally could  not  breathe but ben affleck is one-upping  her by telling people he had to have six  crew members zip him up into the bat  suit before filming the most comfortable  one in snyder's cut  might just have been jared leto's joker  whose costume looks so comfortable  even we wouldn't mind trying it on you  might have noticed that his costume and  makeup were  even more simple than what we saw in his  last appearance in suicide squad  snyder says that's because his one scene  takes place in batman's nightmares  batman one major difference between  justice league and snyder cut  how hands-on snyder was as a director  behind the scenes  we're talking like completely into it as  if he was about to film the scene  alongside the actors  in the behind the scenes footage you can  see how he would explain moves and  choreography and placement step by step  to each actor  half the time he was next to them when  the cameras were rolling and we never  even knew  and you can bet he was 100 proud of his  work  so proud that when someone asked him if  he would be using any footage  that joss whedon had shot his response  was i would set it on fire  before i use a single frame that i did  not photograph  some would call him dramatic but we're  choosing to call him dedicated  okay that dedicated attitude he had is  probably what set the tone for how happy  and laid-back set life was for the cast  while they were filming under his  direction  the behind the scenes outtakes and  bloopers will show you just how much of  a family this cast was  however when the dynamic changed with  joss whedon  gal gadot admits that things weren't the  same during the reshoots  when asked how the experience was  working with whedon she said it honestly  wasn't that great  i had my own experience with him which  wa