o longer  enjoyed the music for the original film  so he spent six months creating a score  in the spare bedroom of his home  in the midst of a pandemic impressive he  says  there were days i woke up in the morning  i didn't know how i was going to finish  it  well we're glad he did another perk for  snyder getting his cut on hbo was that  he got to air it in the format he  originally wanted it in  you might have noticed that the 4-part  movie isn't available in widescreen and  only 4-3 it's all part of the creative  vision  and snyder wanted to make sure it'd be  able to be shown on an imac screen one  day  it's already here the truth is snydercut  was never meant to make it to any  screens whatsoever  director zack snyder was signed on to  the original justice league back in  2016.  tragedy struck at home after the passing  of his daughter  he decided to step away and his version  of justice league was re-shot and  reshaped  to match director joss whedon's vision  but when fans heard that there was a  version of justice league that was true  to snyder's vision  they joined forces and petitioned to  have it released  like actually petitioned they managed to  get  thousands of signatures and the support  of ben affleck and amber heard  warner brothers just couldn't deny them  any longer and bourne was the deal with  hbo  if you pay attention you'll see that the  four-part movie is actually  dedicated to snyder's daughter at the  end of the film it reads  for autumn without her this absolutely  would not have happened  snyder's cut on hbo was definitely the  better option for the footage than what  was originally going to happen with it  snyder admits he was just gonna use it  as some cool videos on his laptop to  share with friends  you see i believe enemies are coming  stop right there i'm in  no one can say there wasn't a tremendous  amount of effort from not only snyder  and his crew  but the fans of the dc universe this  project is the actual definition  of dedi